(3652641, 509225, 65234, '<td valign="top">Great capture; looks like it should be in a sports magazine.  Would have preferred the catcher not be missing his rear, but it doesn''t spoil the shot for me.</td>', 'Great capture; looks like it should be in a sports magazine.  Would have preferred the catcher not be missing his rear, but it doesn''t spoil the shot for me.', '2007-05-15 19:42:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(3652646, 506837, 65234, '<td valign="top">Great shot; nice form on the jumper (but what do I know, I was a track mom but never participated myself).  He looks to be having a great time.  DOF and stop-action keeps this from looking snapshotty despite the other kids in the background.</td>', 'Great shot; nice form on the jumper (but what do I know, I was a track mom but never participated myself).  He looks to be having a great time.  DOF and stop-action keeps this from looking snapshotty despite the other kids in the background.', '2007-05-15 19:43:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(3652662, 509175, 65234, '<td valign="top">Looks like the shots were consumed before the first move; should be an interesting game.  I would try softer, directed lighting to minimize all the reflections and focus the viewer''s attention.</td>', 'Looks like the shots were consumed before the first move; should be an interesting game.  I would try softer, directed lighting to minimize all the reflections and focus the viewer''s attention.', '2007-05-15 19:47:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(3652675, 509164, 78541, '<td valign="top">no way</td>', 'no way', '2007-05-15 19:52:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(3652710, 509286, 71834, '<td valign="top">Stunning shot! One that Billy McConnell would be glad to have for posterity I would have thought. Great panning, shutter speed just right to show some motion in the background and the wheels, but still sharp where it counts.<br/> <br/>I''d love to know which cicuit and how you got so close. Long lens with tight crop or did you manage better access (and how)?</td>', 'Stunning shot! One that Billy McConnell would be glad to have for posterity I would have thought. Great panning, shutter speed just right to show some motion in the background and the wheels, but still sharp where it counts. I''d love to know which cicuit and how you got so close. Long lens with tight crop or did you manage better access (and how)?', '2007-05-15 20:04:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(3652719, 507159, 71834, '<td valign="top">Loses a couple of points for the rotation from vertical, not haing the rider fully in shot and the fast shutter speed freezing the wheels. <br/> <br/>However, from trying to take such photos myself good marks for getting something this good.</td>', 'Loses a couple of points for the rotation from vertical, not haing the rider fully in shot and the fast shutter speed freezing the wheels.  However, from trying to take such photos myself good marks for getting something this good.', '2007-05-15 20:08:26.000000', NULL, 1),
