(3671735, 507805, 31534, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>First Impression is OUCH! <br/> <br/>Technically, Sharp, a little shine on the back drop, but otherwise ok.<br/> <br/>Composition, I would have perfered the shot from a different angle, probably not possible. Could have had a tighter crop.<br/> <br/>Editing, can not really tell if you did anymore than desat. <br/> <br/>Overall, this reminds me of photojournalism shot, would do well in the local paper. <br/> <br/>Best of luck with Olympic shooting, that must be very exciting<br/> <br/>Karen</td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club First Impression is OUCH!  Technically, Sharp, a little shine on the back drop, but otherwise ok. Composition, I would have perfered the shot from a different angle, probably not possible. Could have had a tighter crop. Editing, can not really tell if you did anymore than desat.  Overall, this reminds me of photojournalism shot, would do well in the local paper.  Best of luck with Olympic shooting, that must be very exciting Karen', '2007-05-21 00:50:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(3671822, 509456, 73452, '<td valign="top">This is an amazing photo, and to see it taken in Utah just makes me feel even better! lol!  Fantastic job and congrats on the ribbon!  Well deserved!</td>', 'This is an amazing photo, and to see it taken in Utah just makes me feel even better! lol!  Fantastic job and congrats on the ribbon!  Well deserved!', '2007-05-21 01:01:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3672577, 508561, 51379, '<td valign="top">Thomas, I never got a chance to vote in this challenge,however this shot stuck out for me! Contrary to all the comments having the ball sitting "up" denotes Action to me,its part of the game of golf,and golf is a sport (my favorite)<br/>As far as the ball in focus or a getting a little more detail on it is totally possible without more shots. I see that your  f stop or aperture was set on 2.8, if this were higher on your 20D like f22 or higher your depth of feild will be deeper and a lot more detail will come out in the ball as well as the grass behind the club,of course you''ll have to compensate with a longer/slower shutter speed to get the correct exposure<br/>I like how the club is sitting down in the grass ( just as a 3 wood should) thats how they''re designed. The card for the sky was very creative I''m going to try that on a cloudy day..keep up the good work and don''t worry too much about comments I think we all get them from people who just don''t know.</td>', 'Thomas, I never got a chance to vote in this challenge,however this shot stuck out for me! Contrary to all the comments having the ball sitting "up" denotes Action to me,its part of the game of golf,and golf is a sport (my favorite)As far as the ball in focus or a getting a little more detail on it is totally possible without more shots. I see that your  f stop or aperture was set on 2.8, if this were higher on your 20D like f22 or higher your depth of feild will be deeper and a lot more detail will come out in the ball as well as the grass behind the club,of course you''ll have to compensate with a longer/slower shutter speed to get the correct exposureI like how the club is sitting down in the grass ( just as a 3 wood should) thats how they''re designed. The card for the sky was very creative I''m going to try that on a cloudy day..keep up the good work and don''t worry too much about comments I think we all get them from people who just don''t know.', '2007-05-21 02:57:04.000000', NULL, 0),
