(3681182, 509286, 4411, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by A1EX8:</b></div><hr/><i> As a visitor of *most* of the british superbike meetings, im always trying to get shots like that, i think its spot on.  Do you by any chance have a website with any tips or tricks for an entheusiastic, but never quite getting ''the'' shot, amateur.</i></td></tr></table> <br/>No website, but here''s my 3 step plan ...<br/>1. Your pan should be like a golf swing, smooth and make sure you follow through.<br/>2. Practice.<br/>3. Repeat 2 ad infinitum!<br/> <br/>I could have sworn there was a sports tutorial on this site but I can''t find it now!</td>', 'Originally posted by A1EX8: As a visitor of *most* of the british superbike meetings, im always trying to get shots like that, i think its spot on.  Do you by any chance have a website with any tips or tricks for an entheusiastic, but never quite getting ''the'' shot, amateur. No website, but here''s my 3 step plan ...1. Your pan should be like a golf swing, smooth and make sure you follow through.2. Practice.3. Repeat 2 ad infinitum! I could have sworn there was a sports tutorial on this site but I can''t find it now!', '2007-05-22 18:48:56.000000', NULL, 0),
