(3746458, 507247, 61961, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mmario:</b></div><hr/><i> Great; but <b>this photo is not yours</b>, right?! Autor is <b>Senn</b> from Croatia. <a href="//www.hrphotocontest.com/index.php?menu=7&amp;img=36789" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.hrphotocontest.com/index.php?menu=7&amp;img=36789</a> </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>UNbelievable!  :-/</td>', 'Originally posted by mmario: Great; but this photo is not yours, right?! Autor is Senn from Croatia. //www.hrphotocontest.com/index.php?menu=7&img=36789   UNbelievable!  :-/', '2007-06-06 11:15:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(3788731, 506934, 19978, '<td valign="top">This is seriously one of the best action shots I''ve ever seen. You were robbed! OK, the shadows on her face are a downer, but man, look at that captured moment; the tension of her about to go into her throw, the bitten tongue and determination, the perfect symmetry of her arms and legs. Straight to the faves dude, excellent shot!</td>', 'This is seriously one of the best action shots I''ve ever seen. You were robbed! OK, the shadows on her face are a downer, but man, look at that captured moment; the tension of her about to go into her throw, the bitten tongue and determination, the perfect symmetry of her arms and legs. Straight to the faves dude, excellent shot!', '2007-06-15 16:34:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(3789063, 508388, 33361, '<td valign="top">Really nice sports shot G!</td>', 'Really nice sports shot G!', '2007-06-15 18:17:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(3813632, 509438, 27482, '<td valign="top">Kindof agree with everything khdoss is saying, looks like you "need" a faster lens for this type of photography, I haven´t shot much basketball but the little I know about photographing the sport, you usually have to have a minimum shutter speed of about 1/250 to safely "freeze" the action and especiall the ball, preferrably 1/500 and up.<br/> <br/>Did you shoot this raw?  If you do, try setting the ISO to 1600, overexpose the shot about half a stop and then darken in raw conversion, it will really help with the noise.  Also the white balance is a bit off for my taste, too yellow, try setting the WB to tungsten next time or adjust it afterwards if you  shoot raw.<br/> <br/>Personally I don´t think it´s neccesary to get a new lens, I would just have gone further with the panning and have fun with that, when panning fast sports like basketball I find a shutter of about 1/25 +/- 1 stop works best, depends on what the players are doing.  <br/> <br/>This looks promising so keep it up dude!</td>', 'Kindof agree with everything khdoss is saying, looks like you "need" a faster lens for this type of photography, I haven´t shot much basketball but the little I know about photographing the sport, you usually have to have a minimum shutter speed of about 1/250 to safely "freeze" the action and especiall the ball, preferrably 1/500 and up. Did you shoot this raw?  If you do, try setting the ISO to 1600, overexpose the shot about half a stop and then darken in raw conversion, it will really help with the noise.  Also the white balance is a bit off for my taste, too yellow, try setting the WB to tungsten next time or adjust it afterwards if you  shoot raw. Personally I don´t think it´s neccesary to get a new lens, I would just have gone further with the panning and have fun with that, when panning fast sports like basketball I find a shutter of about 1/25 +/- 1 stop works best, depends on what the players are doing.   This looks promising so keep it up dude!', '2007-06-21 07:37:19.000000', NULL, 0),
